.\" cheval(1) - keep the version below in step with Cargo.toml (a test checks it).
.TH CHEVAL 1 "2026-11-13" "cheval 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.\" File names and settings must not be hyphenated.
.nh
.SH NAME
cheval \- consistent, verified APT repository mirroring with a terminal UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cheval
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-logo
.IR MODE ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cheval
mirrors APT repositories (Debian, Ubuntu and third-party ones such as GitLab, Docker or
NVIDIA) to a local directory that can be served to clients, online or offline.
It replaces
.BR apt\-mirror (1)
and Refrapt and reads one TOML configuration file.
.PP
A mirror is never left half-updated.
For every suite cheval fetches the signed Release file and the indices into a private
staging area, downloads and checksums every package the indices reference, and only then
publishes the suite's
.I dists/
tree, with
.I InRelease
written last.
Consequences worth knowing:
.IP \(bu 2
During a run, and on a first run for as long as packages are still downloading,
.I pool/
fills while
.I dists/
is absent or unchanged.
This is intended.
.IP \(bu 2
A suite with a package that could not be fetched is not published and keeps its previous
state; the run exits with status 1.
.IP \(bu 2
Interrupted downloads resume on the next run.
.IP \(bu 2
Obsolete files are removed only after every repository sharing a directory completed, and
never more than
.B clean_max_percent
of a tree at once.
.PP
The mirror tree is
.IR base_path /mirror/ host / path ,
the layout apt-mirror uses, so an existing tree can be adopted.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Configuration file.
Default:
.BR $CHEVAL_CONFIG ,
then
.IR ./cheval.toml ,
then
.IR /etc/cheval/cheval.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-logo " MODE"
.BR auto " (Unicode in a UTF-8 locale, ASCII otherwise),"
.BR unicode ,
.BR ascii " or"
.BR off .
Also set by
.BR $CHEVAL_LOGO ;
the option wins.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version as one line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help for cheval or for a command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Mirroring
.TP
.B sync \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Mirror the configured repositories.
Shows the terminal UI on a terminal and plain log lines otherwise.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Fetch indices, report what would be downloaded, publish nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Only this repository (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-recheck " size" | hash
Trust existing files whose size matches (default), or re-hash every one.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-clean ", " \-\-force\-clean
Skip cleaning this run, or clean even above
.BR clean_max_percent .
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-tui ", " \-\-exit\-when\-done ", " \-v
Plain output; leave the UI when finished; log retries and per-index details.
.RE
.TP
.B daemon \fR[\fB\-\-run\-on\-start\fR]
Stay up, run syncs on the
.B [daemon]
schedule, and keep the status streams and the HTTP API alive between runs.
.B SIGUSR1
starts a run now;
.B SIGTERM
stops cleanly.
The configuration is re-read before each run.
.TP
.B verify \fR[\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]
Check the local mirror offline against its signed indices: presence and size, or with
.B \-\-full
every checksum.
.TP
.B check
Validate the configuration and show what would be mirrored where.
.SS Setting up
.TP
.B example
Print an annotated example configuration.
.TP
.B probe \fIURL\fR [\fISUITE\fR...]
Inspect an unknown repository and print a suggested
.B [[repo]]
block.
Options:
.BI \-\-user\-agent " UA"
.RB ( apt
impersonates apt),
.BI \-\-username " USER" ,
.BI \-\-password\-env " VAR" ,
.BR \-\-bearer .
.TP
.B import \fR[\fIFILE\fR...]
Convert
.IR sources.list ,
deb822
.IR *.sources ,
apt-mirror
.I mirror.list
or a Refrapt configuration to cheval TOML.
Options:
.BI \-\-base\-path " DIR" ,
.BI \-\-arch " ARCH" .
.TP
.B sources \-\-base\-url \fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-deb822\fR]
Print the apt sources clients need to use this mirror, served under
.IR URL .
.SS Copies and offline transfer
.TP
.B snapshot create \fR[\fINAME\fR] | \fBlist\fR | \fBdelete\fR \fINAME\fR
Hard-linked point-in-time copies of the mirror under
.IR base_path /snapshots.
.TP
.B bundle create \fIOUT.tar\fR [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]... [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-manifest\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Pack what changed since the previous bundle into a tar file to carry across an air gap.
The first bundle is complete; later ones hold only changes and deletions.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Bundle only this repository (repeatable); default is the whole mirror.
Repositories that share a mirror directory must be named together.
Per-repository and whole-mirror bundles can be mixed: one manifest records what the
destination has, and each bundle updates only its own part.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Ignore the manifest and pack everything in reach.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest " FILE"
Record of what the destination has (default
.IR state/bundle\-manifest.tsv ).
Use one per destination site.
.RE
.TP
.B bundle apply \fIIN.tar\fR [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-deleted\fR]
Unpack a bundle into the mirror directory of the offline side.
Packages are written first and Release files last; apply bundles in the order they were
made.
A per-repository bundle cannot write or delete outside its repository's directory.
.SS Status across a one-way link
.TP
.B status listen \fR[\fIURL\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Receive the status stream (default
.BR udp://0.0.0.0:5515 ;
.B tcp://
for a diode TCP proxy), show a read-only progress screen and serve the HTTP API.
Needs no configuration file.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-http " ADDRESS:PORT"
Serve the read-only HTTP API.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Bearer token clients must send; required when
.B \-\-http
is not a loopback address.
.TP
.BI \-\-hmac\-key\-file " FILE"
Accept only messages signed with this key (the sink's
.BR hmac_key_file ).
.TP
.BI \-\-forward " udp://HOST:PORT"
Pass every accepted message on (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-stale\-after " SECONDS"
Report the sender as stale after this much silence (default 180).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tui
Print status lines instead of the screen.
.RE
.TP
.BR version ", " about
Logo, version and build target.
.SH CONFIGURATION
One TOML file.
.B cheval example
prints every setting with comments; the most used are below.
.SS [global]
.TP
.B base_path
Everything lives below it:
.IR mirror/ ,
.IR staging/ ,
.IR state/ ,
.IR snapshots/ ,
.IR log/ .
.TP
.BR threads ", " per_host ", " repo_parallel ", " retries ", " rate_limit
Download concurrency overall and per upstream host, repositories in parallel, retries per
file, and a byte-per-second limit such as "20M".
.TP
.BR proxy ", " ca_bundle ", " user_agent
HTTP proxy, extra CA certificates, user agent ("apt" impersonates apt).
.TP
.BR architectures ", " source
Defaults for every repository.
.TP
.BR verify " = require | auto | off"
Signature checking;
.B auto
verifies when a repository has a
.BR keyring .
.TP
.BR clean " = delete | report | off, " clean_max_percent ", " by_hash_keep_days
What to do with obsolete files.
.TP
.BR recheck ", " check_valid_until
Re-hash existing files each run; refuse expired Release files.
.SS [[repo]]
.TP
.BR name ", " url ", " suites ", " components ", " architectures
What to mirror.
A suite ending in "/" (for example "./") is a flat repository without a
.I dists/
tree.
.TP
.BR keyring ", " verify
OpenPGP keyring for this repository's Release signatures.
.TP
.BR include_packages ", " exclude_packages ", " exclude_paths ", " ignore_missing
Regular expressions: filter by package name or path, or tolerate files the index lists
but upstream no longer has.
.TP
.BR languages ", " installer ", " pdiffs ", " source ", " extra_files
Optional index and file selection.
.TP
.BR mirror_dir ", " enabled ", " user_agent ", " check_valid_until ", " publish_partial
Per-repository overrides.
.TP
.B [repo.auth]
.BR username ,
.B password_env
or
.BR password_file ,
.BR bearer ,
.BR headers ,
.BR client_cert .
.SS [daemon]
.TP
.B schedule
Daily local times ("03:17" or "03:17,15:17") or an interval ("6h", "30m").
.TP
.B run_on_start
Also run when the daemon starts.
.SS [status], [[status.sink]], [status.http]
Monitoring only; no mirror content is ever sent.
.TP
.BR interval_ms ", " heartbeat_secs ", " host
Progress cadence during a run, idle heartbeat cadence, host name in messages.
.TP
.B [[status.sink]]
.B url
.RB ( udp://host:port
or
.BR tcp://host:port ),
.B format
.RB ( json
or
.BR syslog ),
.B repeat
(send each datagram N times),
.BR hmac_key_file ,
.BR facility ,
.BR syslog_progress_secs .
Sinks are send-only; a dead one never delays a sync.
.TP
.B [status.http]
.B listen
(for example "127.0.0.1:8611"),
.B token
or
.BR token_file .
Endpoints:
.IR /v1/status ,
.IR /v1/repos ,
.IR /v1/events ,
.IR /v1/stream ,
.IR /healthz ,
.IR /metrics .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start from the template, check it, see the size, then mirror:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval example > /etc/cheval/cheval.toml
cheval check
cheval sync \-\-dry\-run
cheval sync
.EE
.RE
.PP
A minimal configuration:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
[global]
base_path = "/srv/cheval"

[[repo]]
name       = "debian"
url        = "https://deb.debian.org/debian"
suites     = ["trixie", "trixie\-updates"]
components = ["main"]
keyring    = "/usr/share/keyrings/debian\-archive\-keyring.gpg"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Find out how to mirror an unfamiliar repository, or convert an existing setup:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval probe https://packages.gitlab.com/gitlab/gitlab\-ee/debian/trixie
cheval import /etc/apt/sources.list /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
cheval import /etc/apt/mirror.list \-\-base\-path /srv/cheval
.EE
.RE
.PP
Mirror one repository without the UI, then check every file:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval sync \-\-only debian \-\-no\-tui
cheval verify \-\-full \-\-only debian
.EE
.RE
.PP
Serve the mirror and point clients at it (any web server on
.IR base_path /mirror):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval sources \-\-base\-url http://mirror.lan \-\-deb822
.EE
.RE
.PP
Carry the whole mirror, or single repositories, across an air gap:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval bundle create /media/usb/all\-2026\-11\-13.tar
cheval bundle create /media/usb/debian.tar \-\-only debian
cheval bundle create /media/usb/gitlab.tar \-\-only gitlab\-ee\-trixie \e
                                           \-\-only gitlab\-runner\-debian
# on the offline side:
cheval bundle apply /media/usb/debian.tar
cheval verify \-\-full
.EE
.RE
.PP
Keep a point-in-time copy before a risky update:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval snapshot create before\-upgrade
cheval snapshot list
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run as a daemon and ask it how it is doing:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
systemctl enable \-\-now cheval\-daemon
systemctl kill \-s USR1 cheval\-daemon
curl \-s http://127.0.0.1:8611/v1/status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Watch the sending side from the far side of a data diode:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
cheval status listen udp://0.0.0.0:5515 \-\-http 127.0.0.1:8611 \e
       \-\-hmac\-key\-file /etc/cheval/status.key
.EE
.RE
.PP
Cron instead of the daemon or the systemd timer:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
17 3 * * *  cheval \-c /etc/cheval/cheval.toml sync \-\-no\-tui >/dev/null
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The run finished but one or more suites failed (they keep their previous state);
.B verify
found problems.
.TP
.B 2
Error: bad configuration, another instance holds the lock, I/O failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CHEVAL_CONFIG
Configuration file when
.B \-c
is not given.
.TP
.B CHEVAL_LOGO
See
.BR \-\-logo .
.TP
.BR http_proxy ", " https_proxy ", " no_proxy
Used when
.B global.proxy
is not set.
.TP
.I password_env variables
Secrets named by
.B password_env
in
.BR [repo.auth] .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cheval/cheval.toml
Default configuration.
.TP
.IR base_path /mirror/
The tree to serve.
.TP
.IR base_path /state/last\-run.json
Result of the last run, for monitoring.
.TP
.IR base_path /state/bundle\-manifest.tsv
What the bundle destination already has.
.TP
.IR base_path /log/cheval.log
Log of every run.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/cheval/
README, example configuration, and
.I status\-stream.md
(status message, syslog and HTTP API reference).
.TP
.IR cheval.service ", " cheval.timer ", " cheval\-daemon.service ", " cheval\-status\-listen.service
systemd units.
Enable the timer or the daemon, not both.
.SH NOTES
Signature verification does not evaluate key expiry or revocation.
Filtered packages remain listed in the signed indices.
Upstreams are HTTP and HTTPS only.
Without
.BR hmac_key_file ,
anything that can send to a status receiver's port can feed it false status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR apt\-mirror (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Source, releases and issues: https://github.com/nc\-intezra/cheval
